@badal-coder this PR affects the function `wsl.isRunning(<machine-name>)` only. It's a function that isn't used when creating or starting a machine (it is used when stopping it, changing the network mode or checking its state).

Enabling the WSL native systemd support requires editing the file [/etc/wsl.conf](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/systemd#how-to-enable-systemd) in the [Podman machine OS](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman-machine-os).

Anyway, if you want to continue working on this PR we need at least the details of what you are fixing. What Podman scenario is currently failing and is addressed after applying your patch? How can I reproduce it? Are you using a custom podman machine OS image?
